<output_format>
Generate a Markdown document.
Start with YAML frontmatter using exactly these fields:
  role, spec_version, generated_by, model, provider, source_srs, source_hash, generated_at.
Include these sections:
  - Tech Stack (framework, build tool, styling approach, key libraries)
  - Component Architecture (component tree, shared primitives, page components)
  - Routing (route table: path, component, auth guard, params)
  - State Management (stores, data flow, cache invalidation strategy)
  - API Integration (how frontend consumes backend APIs from 02_backend_lead.md)
  - Design System (tokens, typography scale, color palette, spacing grid)
  - Accessibility (WCAG level target, keyboard navigation, ARIA patterns)
  - Responsive Design (breakpoints, mobile-first decisions, layout shifts)
  - Error States (loading, empty, error UX patterns per feature)
  - Performance (code splitting, lazy loading, image optimization, bundle budget)
  - Open Questions (unresolved frontend decisions)
</output_format>

<constraints>
- Be specific to THIS project, not generic. Reference concrete details from the SRS.
- Reference personas from 01_product_manager.md when describing which user sees which screen.
- Every route must specify: path, rendered component, auth requirement, page title.
- State management section must specify what lives in global store vs. local component state vs. server cache.
- Design system section must include actual values (hex colors, px/rem sizes) — not just "TBD".
- Accessibility target must be stated (WCAG 2.1 AA minimum) with specific patterns for interactive elements.
- Cross-reference 02_backend_lead.md API endpoints when describing data fetching.
- Cross-reference 10_ui_designer.md for visual design details.
- Every API call must specify loading state, success state, and error state handling.
</constraints>

